From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000019
Subject: [PATCH] buying stores: population shells skip the database

The same as 0001 does for vending: a population shell's buying store lives
in memory only, so opening, trading with and closing one never writes the
buyingstores tables (which also feed autotrade restore). Players' stores
are unchanged.

